      "reasoning": "My turn 9! I drew Plains. I have Chains of Custody, Plains, Sage's Reverie. No creature.\n\
\n\
I can play Plains (land drop). That's fine.\n\
\n\
I still have no creature to enchant. I need to draw a creature next turn.\n\
\n\
But I'm at 3 life, opponent at 7. They have Rapacious Dragon (untapped next turn), Spiteful Prankster (untapped), Dragon Hatchling (0/1). They can attack with Rapacious Dragon (3/3 flying) and Spiteful Prankster (3/2). That's 6 damage, lethal.\n\
\n\
I need to either remove a creature or gain life or block.\n\
\n\
If I had a creature with flying to block Rapacious Dragon, I could survive. But I have none.\n\
\n\
I could cast Chains of Custody if I had a creature. I need to draw a creature next turn, but they attack before I can cast.\n\
\n\
Thus I need to draw a creature with flash that I can cast during their combat. My deck is white/black, maybe there's a creature with flash? Not likely.\n\
\n\
I could draw a removal spell like Eaten Alive? That's in graveyard.\n\
\n\
I could draw something like Favored of Iroas? That's also in graveyard.\n\
\n\
I need to draw something like Murder? Not in deck.\n\
\n\
My only hope is to draw a creature with flying and cast it before combat, then block.\n\
\n\
But I have no mana to cast both a creature and Chains of Custody.\n\
\n\
Better to just play Plains and pass.\n\
\n\
I'll pass.\n\
\n\
Choose no.\n\
\n\
\n\
